/-!
# Brown hypotheses: ambient localizing category

Source: blueprint main-20261015, sec-six-functors-basics/sk-lem-brown-hypotheses,
node det-brown-hypotheses-ambient (blueprint: det-brown-hypotheses-ambient).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open AlgebraicGeometry Scheme

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale

/--
The localizing category generated by bounded constructible finite-Tor complexes
is locally small and triangulated, has arbitrary small direct sums, and has split
idempotents.  Here `Λ` is one of the admissible condensed coefficient rings
listed in `sk-def-localizing-closure`, with its coefficient data and topology;
`X` is a scheme and all smallness is in the fixed larger universe.
The prime `l`, finite discrete ring `A` with `l`-power zero, and finite subextension
`E` give the coefficient data of that definition. The six alternatives in `_hΛ`
identify `Λ` as a ring object with `A`, `ℤ_[l]`, `𝒪_E`, `ℚ_[l]`, `E`, or
`PadicAlgCl l`, respectively. For the last alternative we use all continuous
maps with the valuation topology, as this node and its localizing-closure source
specify; this is not the finite-subextension-valued condensed ring.

The proof proceeds as follows.  First identify internal modules over the pulled-
back condensed ring with modules over its reconstructed ring sheaf, using the
internal-abelian-sheaf-module equivalence
[def-weil-pbc-internal-abelian-sheaf-module-equivalence] and monoidal sheafification
[sk-def-sfb-sheaf-tensor], preserving the actual pulled-back coefficient ring
[sk-def-sfb-pulled-back-coefficients].  The
small pro-etale skeleton [def-weil-pbc-proetale-site] and the size convention
[def-weil-size-convention] provide the required universe
hypotheses.  The sectionwise ring-sheaf module theorem then makes the module
category Grothendieck abelian [lem-weil-pbc-ring-sheaves-grothendieck]; the equivalence transports
colimits, kernels,
cokernels, exact filtered colimits, and a generator, and the Grothendieck
K-injective theorem [lem-sfb-grothendieck-k-injective] supplies resolutions.

Represent `K` and `L` by complexes and resolve the latter K-injectively.  The
K-injective derived-Hom comparison [lem-weil-pbc-kinjective-hom-derived] identifies their Hom with
chain-homotopy
classes of maps, a set because the site and all values lie in the fixed
universe.  Thus the full localizing subcategory is locally small.  The ambient
derived category is triangulated and has termwise coproducts by the
Grothendieck-derived-coproduct theorem [lem-kun-grothendieck-derived-coproducts],
using the unbounded localization [def-weil-abstract-derived-category].  The intersection
definition of the
localizing closure [sk-def-localizing-closure] inherits the triangulation
[def-weil-triangulated-subcategory] and the coproduct universal
property, including the empty sum.  Finally, the countable-coproduct
idempotent-completeness theorem [lem-countable-coproducts-idempotent-complete] applied inside this
localizing subcategory gives
an object and maps splitting every idempotent.

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 05QW; blueprint node det-brown-hypotheses-ambient,
steps 1--6 (blueprint: det-brown-hypotheses-ambient).
-/
theorem det_brown_hypotheses_ambient
    (l : ℕ) [Fact l.Prime]
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Finite A] [TopologicalSpace A] [DiscreteTopology A]
    (_hA : ∃ n : ℕ, (l ^ n : A) = 0)
    (E : PadicAlgCl.FiniteIntermediateField l)
    (Λ : Sheaf (coherentTopology Profinite.{u}) Ab.{u + 1})
    [MonObj Λ] [IsCommMonObj Λ]
    (_hΛ :
      Nonempty (Mon.mk Λ ≅ Mon.mk (Profinite.continuousCoefficientRingObj A)) ∨
      Nonempty (Mon.mk Λ ≅ Mon.mk (Profinite.continuousMapRingObj ℤ_[l])) ∨
      Nonempty (Mon.mk Λ ≅ Mon.mk (Profinite.padicIntegersRingObj l E)) ∨
      Nonempty (Mon.mk Λ ≅ Mon.mk (Profinite.continuousMapRingObj ℚ_[l])) ∨
      Nonempty (Mon.mk Λ ≅ Mon.mk (Profinite.continuousMapRingObj E)) ∨
      Nonempty (Mon.mk Λ ≅ Mon.mk (Profinite.continuousMapRingObj (PadicAlgCl l))))
    (X : Scheme.{u}) :
    LocallySmall.{u + 1} (localizingClosureProEtale Λ X).FullSubcategory ∧
      (localizingClosureProEtale Λ X).IsTriangulated ∧
      HasCoproducts.{u + 1} (localizingClosureProEtale Λ X).FullSubcategory ∧
      IsIdempotentComplete (localizingClosureProEtale Λ X).FullSubcategory := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale
